@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>This is a starting draft, not certified legal text — have it reviewed before relying on it.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>
    At this stage, CarShell collects the admin's own login through Supabase Auth, and whatever a
    seller's listing exposes publicly, which is a postcode, not a full address. There are no buyer
    accounts yet, so there's no buyer data to protect beyond basic request logs.
</p>

<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
<p>
    The admin's account data rests on contract: they're using the service. Request logging rests
    on legitimate interest, for security and operations.
</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
    Application logs roll off after 90 days. A removed listing's rows and images stay for a stated
    period for dispute or record purposes, then get purged, rather than living forever with no
    policy at all.
</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>Contact the site operator directly with any questions about this policy.</p>
